ype":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{0,79}$"}},"reason":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500},"fasteners":{"type":"array","maxItems":8,"description":"What holds this joint: catalog items with a fastener kind, in any mix; empty while nothing is chosen. count and spacing_mm follow how the item is counted: along the contact, a null count lets the database count and space it; per joint, give the count and no spacing; per construction, both stay null.","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["material_id","material_revision","count","spacing_mm"],"properties":{"material_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"material_revision":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":999999999},"count":{"anyOf":[{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":10000},{"type":"null"}]},"spacing_mm":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":2000},{"type":"null"}]}}}},"except":{"type":"array","maxItems":64,"description":"Part id pairs this rule does not join, e.g. a part that rests, slides or is removable.","items":{"type":"array","minItems":2,"maxItems":2,"items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{0,79}$"}}}}}},"form_assign":{"type":"array","maxItems":128,"description":"The concept component for a part that several components hold. Code maps every other part itself; empty for none.","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"instance_id":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.:-]{0,79}$"},"component_id":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,31}$"}},"required":["instance_id","component_id"]}}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Change only named parts and their dependencies in an exact saved construction. Omit unchanged collections and posts. Each included collection has upsert (complete changed/new posts) and remove (existing IDs, or binding paths); no ID may appear in both. The server merges with the saved revision and preserves everything else. Explicitly remove or update dependent joints, bindings, nodes, materials and roles when removing parts; no silent cascade. Keep stable identity: a joint with different endpoints needs a new ID. New instance roles need evidence, or explicit unknown/unknown. For existing numeric input values use change_construction_parameters; for role-only changes use change_construction_roles. Reuse key only for an exact retry; corrected input needs a new key. The saved result includes the whole-model check of the receipt revision; complete its affected outputs; this is not a drawing receipt. solution_edit:null changes only the Construction. Otherwise supply the selected Solution edit_ref, content changes and reason to update that Solution/selection and this Construction atomically; the server binds the new selection. Uses the same content paths as edit_project_record, preserves sources/identities and resets design alignment to draft unless /design_intent/alignment is explicitly set. The whole change rolls back on failure and exact key replay returns the original receipts. text:null keeps the saved title and description. When either states a size this change alters, supply text with the complete corrected title and description (or leave sizes out of them); a change that would leave a stated overall size wrong is rejected without saving. text.open_questions:null preserves saved questions; a supplied complete list replaces them (empty clears). A text-only edit may use an empty instances delta. Correct stale questions in the same bounded edit; source and geometry guards still apply. mode sketch keeps this change in your sketch of the construction instead of saving it: it is merged with the changes already sketched (a later change to the same id replaces the earlier one), checked as a whole like a saved revision, and saves nothing. expected_revision stays the saved revision the sketch started from. mode save saves at once. Build a construction in the sketch and save it once with commit_construction_sketch when the assignment is done, or at a step the owner should see. Lean writing: a number in an upserted definition or part may be a formula over parameter node names; code adds its nodes and bindings and removes formula nodes nothing uses any more. joint_rules joins touching parts by definition pair; code writes the joints for touching pairs that have none. Code maps an added part to the concept component whose envelope holds it, when exactly one does, and drops removed ones; form_assign names the component for a part several hold. Joints code wrote follow their parts when they move. A change refused only for a text, a formula or a joint rule is kept in your sketch: send only the correction with mode sketch, then commit it.","expected_return":{"format":"json","contract":"The registered handler returns its structured domain result and status; a successful write additionally returns its saved receipt. A provider tool call alone is not a saved result."},"card_description":"Use when named parts of a saved Construction change in shape, material, formula or joints, or parts are added or removed. Gives a merged new revision with everything else kept and its whole-model check; value-only changes use change_construction_parameters. Can update the selected Solution atomically.","optional_parameters":[],"required_parameters":["key","record_id","expected_revision","change_note","request_quote","changes","solution_edit","text","mode","joint_rules","form_assign"],"additional_description":"Read the exact revision and relevant stable IDs. Send only changed collections with explicit upserts/removals; preserve unrelated parts. Resolve dependent bindings, nodes, joints, materials and roles explicitly. Keep unknown evidence unknown. Use parameter/role commands for those narrower changes. Corrected input gets a new key; exact retry reuses its receipt. The saved result includes the check of that revision; read_construction_changes before drawing or claiming completion."}$lean_edit$::jsonb,
    'tools.commit_construction_sketch',$lean_commit${"name":"commit_construction_sketch","handler":"commit_construction_sketch","envelope":{"type":"function","arguments":"JSON object validated against parameters; project binding and write provenance remain server-owned.","schema_version":1},"parameters":{"type":"object","required":["record_id","new_key","action","key","change_note","request_quote"],"properties":{"key":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}$"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"commit and rebase: names this change; a corrected retry needs a new key. null for read and discard."},"action":{"enum":["commit","read","discard","rebase"],"type":"string"},"new_key":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,80}$"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The key of a save_construction_draft sketch; null for an edit_construction_parts sketch."},"record_id":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"The construction the sketch belongs to; null for a new construction."},"change_note":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":1000,"minLength":1},{"type":"null"}],"description":"commit and rebase: what the saved change does, in plain words. null for read and discard."},"request_quote":{"type":"string","maxLength":500,"minLength":1}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Save, read or discard your sketch of one construction. new_key is the key of a sketch made with save_construction_draft (a new construction, or a whole revision of a saved one); for a sketch made with edit_construction_parts new_key is null. commit saves all sketched changes as one revision, a new construction as revision 1, through the same checks as a direct save, with the whole-model check of that revision. read shows what the sketch holds. discard drops it without saving. rebase moves an edit_construction_parts sketch onto the current saved revision when the construction changed after the sketch began, and checks it there. A sketch lasts for this request only.","expected_return":{"format":"json","contract":"The registered handler returns its structured domain result and status; a successful write additionally returns its saved receipt. A provider tool call alone is not a saved result."},"card_description":"Use to save, read or discard the sketch of construction changes made with edit_construction_parts mode sketch, or of a new construction sketched with save_construction_draft mode sketch. A commit saves them as one revision with its whole-model check.","optional_parameters":[],"required_parameters":["record_id","new_key","action","key","change_note","request_quote"],"additional_description":"Commit once when the assignment is done, or at a step the owner should see: the construction then gets one new revision, its whole-model check and its follow-up work once. Read the sketch first when unsure what it holds. When a commit says the construction changed, rebase, correct what the rebase names with edit_construction_parts mode sketch, then commit."}$lean_commit$::jsonb);
  hashes jsonb:='{"tools.save_construction_draft":"da7569b2eaed8bedf050aac83ea03b29","tools.edit_construction_parts":"014bf10d5cb0b94ff5f4d99771883781","tools.commit_construction_sketch":"307403bd164bad8ddf641b92544ea8ae"}'::jsonb;
begin
  perform pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtextextended('ai_catalog:bob',0));
  foreach tool in array array['tools.save_construction_draft','tools.edit_construction_parts','tools.commit_construction_sketch'] loop
    select v.* into prior from shared.ai_prompts p
      join shared.ai_prompt_versions v on v.id=p.active_version_id
      where p.app='bob' and p.prompt_key=tool and p.definition_kind='tool_contract' and p.retired_at is null for update of p;
    expected:=hashes->>tool;
    if not found or md5(prior.definition::text)<>expected or prior.metadata->>'publication' is distinct from 'bob-lean-writes-v1'
      or prior.metadata ? 'lean_construction_version' then
      raise exception 'lean_construction_tool_unexpected: %',tool;
    end if;
    def:=defs->tool;
    select coalesce(max(version),0)+1 into next_version from shared.ai_prompt_versions where prompt_id=prior.prompt_id;
    insert into shared.ai_prompt_versions(prompt_id,version,definition_kind,definition_format_version,metadata,content,definition,flow,available_variables)
      values(prior.prompt_id,next_version,prior.definition_kind,prior.definition_format_version,
        (prior.metadata-'seed_version'-'source_revision')||'{"publication":"bob-lean-construction-v1","lean_construction_version":1}'::jsonb,
        prior.content,def,prior.flow,prior.available_variables)
    returning id into version_uuid;
    activation:=activation||jsonb_build_object(tool,version_uuid);
  end loop;
  perform shared.activate_ai_catalog('bob',activation);
end $bob_lean_construction$;
commit;
